# Ported from the previous hand-written reference test: a stable capture of the
# installed CLI's non-interactive help header. No credentials, no network, no
# version-dependent subprocess.
rows 4
cols 120
why CR returns to column one and LF opens the next row, so three CRLF-separated
why lines occupy rows one to three and leave the cursor at the start of row four.
stream Usage: claude [options] [command] [prompt]\r\n
stream Claude Code - starts an interactive session by default, use -p/--print for\r\n
stream non-interactive output\r\n
cursor 3 0
line Usage: claude [options] [command] [prompt]
line Claude Code - starts an interactive session by default, use -p/--print for
line non-interactive output
line
